  "result": "Excellent! The late fee function has been successfully implemented. Here's what was added:\n\n**src/reports.js** \u2014 Added `lateFee(invoice, asOf)` function that:\n- Returns 0 if invoice is not overdue (dueDate >= asOf)\n- Calculates days overdue using `daysBetween(dueDate, asOf)`\n- Uses `balanceDue(invoice)` to get the remaining amount owed\n- Computes late fee as: amountDue \u00d7 daysOverdue \u00d7 0.0004 (which is 0.04% per day)\n- Returns the fee rounded to integer cents using `roundCents()`\n\n**test/reports.test.js** \u2014 Added 15 comprehensive tests covering:\n- Not yet overdue \u2192 returns 0\n- Exact due date \u2192 returns 0\n- Fully paid invoices \u2192 returns 0\n- Single day overdue with correct calculation\n- Multiple days overdue with correct calculation\n- Partially paid invoices use remaining balance\n- Large amounts and many days\n- Proper integer cent rounding\n- Zero amount due \u2192 returns 0\n- Fees increase with more days overdue\n- Proportionality to amount due\n- Different payment terms\n- Transition from 0 to positive fee day after due date\n\n**All 248 tests pass** \u2713",
